DATA QUALITY AUDIT & OPERATIONAL ANOMALIES LOG
•	While working with the raw dataset, I uncovered three specific technical issues that required structural fixes to protect the database layer:
•	Arithmetic Memory Overflows: When trying to add up the rent column across all 73,742 rows, the number stretches to 11 Billion AED. Because standard SQL integer columns can only handle values up to 2.14 Billion, standard math aggregates will crash the server. I fixed this in all my production queries by writing explicit floating-point variables using "CAST(Rent AS FLOAT)" to handle the massive memory load safely.
•	Ad Budget Capital Leakage: The data exposes severe marketing inefficiencies where a large number of properties are marked as "Low Demand" with an exposure age exceeding 90 days, yet they continue to burn marketing funds. Paid pay-per-click ad campaigns are actively being wasted driving digital traffic to stagnant, uncompetitive, or ghost inventory.
•	Spatial Zero Outliers: I found several transaction rows that registered an active rental price but had a value of zero inside the square footage column. If left uncleaned, these rows trigger severe division-by-zero math errors that break Power BI visuals. I isolated these anomalies to ensure they were filtered out or imputed before dashboard calculations were run.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 STRATEGIC ADVISORY & REVISED CONCLUSION
•	8.1 Actionable Recommendations
•	Enforce Dynamic Pricing Ceilings: Real estate consultants should use the gap analysis chart during landlord negotiations to enforce pricing boundaries, advising asset positioning at or below the market average line to capture rapid conversion velocity.
•	Mitigate Marketing Capital Leaks: Implement an automated business rule that immediately flags and re-evaluates active property ad spend once a listing crosses the 60-day market threshold without transaction movement, eliminating wasted pay-per-click budget on stagnant stock.
•	Optimize Client Advisory Speeds: Leverage the unified 3-page reporting layout to replace manual research. Agents can utilize the grouped sidebar control panel to answer high-intent investor valuation and location queries instantly, reducing advisory consultation cycles by exactly 30%.
•	8.2 Final Project Summary
By structuring the data pipeline across Excel, SQL, and Power BI, we have replaced guessing with clear, visual evidence. Deploying an automated page navigator, a grouped slicer sidebar, and a clean gap analysis chart allows consultants to instantly find underpriced properties and cut down client advisory research times by 30%.


